Limerence: an involuntary state of intense romantic fixation—craving another person’s attention, searching every interaction for signs, idealizing them, and swinging between euphoria and anxiety depending on perceived reciprocation.

It isn’t quite love. Love increasingly sees the whole person; limerence feeds on uncertainty, projection, and possibility. The less certain the bond, the more violently the mind may try to resolve it.

Pantheon shorthand:

desire + uncertainty + intermittent reward → recursive attention capture

Or more simply: longing caught in a feedback loop.